          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong category of cubes
            is a category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+shapes+for+higher+structures"} geometric shapes for higher structures
            in which the basic shapes are cubes of all dimensions. There are actually many different categories of cubes, depending on what sorts of operations are permitted between cubes. In general, we expect the following of a category of cubes:
          %ul
            %li
              It is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo □
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Box,\otimes,I^0)
              = succeed "-cube\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-cube\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              = succeed "-cube\u201D," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mi m
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+m)
              = succeed "-cube\u201D" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi I
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^{0}
            %li
              It contains an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I^{1}
              with two “faces”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_0, \delta_1 \colon I^{0} \to I^{1}
              and a “degeneracy”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi I
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon \colon I^{1} \to I^{0}
              fitting in the diagram below.
          %svg{:height => "89.164pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 191.614 89.164", :width => "191.614pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
